        q: 'What does a cat\'s purring sound like, and when do you hear it?',
        a: 'Purring is a low, rumbling vibration cats make by rapidly opening and closing the muscles in their voice box as they breathe in and out. You most often hear it when a cat is being stroked, is relaxed, or sometimes when it is unwell.',
