        q: 'Where did the domestic cat originally come from, and where is it most biologically diverse?',
        a: 'Domestic cats descend from the Near Eastern wildcat (Felis silvestris lybica), first domesticated in the Fertile Crescent around 10,000 years ago alongside agriculture. Genetic diversity is highest in the Middle East, reflecting this origin.',
