        q: 'Where in the world have calico and tortoiseshell cats held specific cultural significance, and what traditions arose?',
        a: 'In Japan, the Maneki-neko (beckoning cat) lucky figurine is almost always depicted as a calico or tortoiseshell, believed to attract wealth and good fortune. In the United States, calico cats were officially designated Maryland\'s state cat in 2001. Maritime communities across Europe considered tortoiseshell cats good luck on ships — sailors believed they brought calm seas, making them highly sought after and deliberately bred for voyages.',
