        a: 'The case for preserving the cat calico rests on multiple arguments: ecological value (its role in maintaining ecosystem services), scientific value (insights into biology and evolution), ethical value (the intrinsic worth of living species), and cultural value. These arguments collectively justify significant conservation investment.',
