        a: 'Early farmers in the Fertile Crescent (modern Syria/Turkey region) approximately 10,000 years ago inadvertently domesticated cats by creating grain stores that attracted rodents, which in turn attracted wildcats. People tolerated and eventually welcomed the cats for pest control — domestication happened through mutual benefit rather than deliberate breeding.',
