        pointer: null,
        q: 'Who was Félicette, and why is she significant to space exploration history?',
        a: 'Félicette was a black-and-white Parisian stray cat who became the first (and only) cat in space when France launched her on 18 October 1963 aboard a Véronique AG1 rocket. She survived the flight and parachuted safely back to Earth. Despite her historical significance, she received little recognition for decades — a bronze statue was finally erected in her honour at the International Space University, Strasbourg, in 2019, funded by a crowdfunding campaign.',
