        difficulty: 'very-hard',
        wh: 'WHEN',
        pointer: null,
        q: 'When were cats first brought to Europe, and how did their role change from practical to symbolic?',
        a: 'Cats reached Europe via trade routes around 4,000 years ago. In ancient Rome they were practical pest controllers; during the medieval period their association with independence and night-time led to superstitions linking them (especially black cats) with witchcraft, which paradoxically boosted rodent populations and may have worsened the Black Death.',
