        pointer: null,
        q: 'How does an eagle use its beak to eat?',
        a: 'An eagle\'s beak is large and strongly hooked. It cannot chew — instead it uses the sharp tip and curved hook to tear chunks of flesh from prey. The beak is also used to feed meat to chicks in the nest, breaking it into small, manageable pieces.',
