        q: 'Why is equine therapy used to help children with autism and other conditions?',
        a: 'Horses respond to human body language and mood, encouraging children to be calm and aware of their own body. Riding strengthens muscles and improves balance. The bond formed with a horse can build confidence, communication, and emotional regulation in children who find human interaction difficult.',
