        difficulty: 'very-hard',
        wh: 'WHY',
        pointer: null,
        q: 'Why is library use considered a fundamental component of a healthy society?',
        a: 'Library use is fundamental because it contributes to outcomes that societies universally value: health, education, wellbeing, and social cohesion. Its effects extend far beyond individuals to communities and future generations.',
