        difficulty: 'ultimate',
        wh: 'WHEN',
        pointer: null,
        q: 'When do investments in libraries and reading produce the greatest long-term returns, and what does this imply for policy priorities?',
        a: 'The evidence shows that investments in libraries and reading during critical developmental periods — particularly early childhood — produce far greater long-term returns than later interventions. This has profound implications for how societies should prioritise their resources and design social support systems.',
