        a: 'Research increasingly shows that disparities in libraries and reading outcomes reflect structural inequalities — in income, housing, education, power — that cannot be resolved through individual-level interventions alone. Achieving genuine equity requires addressing the systems that produce unequal conditions, not just providing compensatory services to those who have been disadvantaged by those systems.',
