        q: 'Does the growing evidence base in libraries and reading translate effectively into improved practice, and what are the barriers?',
        a: 'The translation of research evidence into improved practice is one of the central challenges of libraries and reading. Barriers include: the time lag between research and dissemination, resistance from practitioners with established practices, organisational factors that prevent adoption of new approaches, and the complexity of adapting findings from controlled research settings to real-world contexts.',
