        a: 'AI offers genuine potential to improve child development and play through better diagnostics, more personalised support, and more efficient service delivery. But it also introduces risks: algorithmic bias, erosion of human relationships, over-reliance on automated decision-making. The outcome depends on how AI is designed, governed, and deployed — which are fundamentally human choices rather than technological inevitabilities.',
